hadiths[39]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3645","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3645 Arabic Hadees: 3079"
"3646","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3646 Arabic Hadees: 1863"
"3647","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3647 Arabic Hadees: 3542"
"3648","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3648 Arabic Hadees: 2934"
"3649","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3649 Arabic Hadees: 2862"
"3650","On the authority of Amir bin Sa'd, he said: Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas was among his camels when his son Umar came to him. When Sa'd saw him, he said: ""I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this rider."" So he dismounted and said to him: ""You stay among your camels and sheep and leave the people disputing over the kingdom among themselves?"" So Sa'd struck him on his chest and said: ""Be quiet! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Indeed Allah loves the servant who is pious, wealthy, and inconspicuous.'""And Kathir bin Zayd al-Aslami narrated it from al-Mutallib from Umar bin Sa'd from his father that he said: His son Amir came to him and said: ""O my son! In the fitnah you command me to be a leader? No, by Allah! Until I am given a sword that if I strike a Muslim with it, it bounces off him, and if I strike a disbeliever with it, it kills him."" I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ... and he mentioned the hadith."
