"3677","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3677 Arabic Hadees: 959"
"3678","Dhayyal ibn Utbah ibn Hanzalah said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Hudhaym, my grandfather, [say] that his grandfather Hanifah said to Hudhaym: ""Gather my sons for me, for I wish to make a bequest."" So he gathered them, and he said: ""The first thing I bequest is that for this orphan of mine who is in my care [there shall be] one hundred camels from those camels which we used to call in the pre-Islamic period 'al-Mutayyibah' (the good/pure ones)."" Hudhaym said: ""O my father! I heard your sons saying: 'We only acknowledge this in our father's presence; when he dies, we will go back on it.'"" He said: ""Then between me and you is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" Hudhaym said: ""We are satisfied."" So Hudhaym, Hanifah, and Hanzalah set out with them, [along with] a boy who was riding behind Hudhaym. When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they greeted him. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""What brought you here, O Abu Hudhaym?"" He said: ""This [matter],"" and he struck his hand on Hudhaym's thigh. He said: ""I feared that old age or death might overtake me suddenly, so I wanted to bequest that for this orphan of mine who is in my care one hundred camels from those camels which we used to call in the pre-Islamic period 'al-Mutayyibah'."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until we saw the anger in his face. He was sitting, so he knelt on his knees and said: ""No, no, no. The charity [due] is five [camels], or else ten, or else fifteen, or else twenty, or else twenty-five, or else thirty, or else thirty-five; if they are many, then forty."" He said: ""So they took leave of him, and with the orphan was a stick with which he was striking a camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'How great is this stick of an orphan!'"" Hanzalah said: ""So he brought me near to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have sons with beards and younger than that, and this one is the youngest of them, so supplicate Allah for him.' He wiped his head and said: 'May Allah bless you' or 'Blessed be you.'"" Dhayyal said: ""I have indeed seen Hanzalah being brought a person with a swollen face or an animal with a swollen udder; he would spit on his hands, say: 'In the name of Allah,' place his hand on its head and say: 'On the spot of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' then wipe it over it."" Dhayyal said: ""And the swelling would go away."""
